flowchart TB
%% Book-palette Mermaid template. Copy the classDef block into any new flowchart
%% and tag nodes with :::class to get the same semantic colors the hand-authored
%% SVGs use, so Mermaid output is on-brand instead of monochrome.
%% Render: py -3 scripts/diagrams/render.py mermaid diagram.mmd diagram.png
%% Palette: input=blue 1e88e5 | good=green 43a047 | bad=red e53935 | process=orange fb8c00 | special=purple 8e24aa
  A[input or start]:::inp --> P{decision?}:::proc
  P -- yes --> G[accepted path]:::good
  P -- no  --> B[rejected path]:::bad
  G --> M[model / special step]:::spec

  classDef inp  fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1e88e5,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#0d47a1;
  classDef good fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#43a047,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#1b5e20;
  classDef bad  fill:#ffebee,stroke:#e53935,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#b71c1c;
  classDef proc fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#fb8c00,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#e65100;
  classDef spec fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#8e24aa,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#4a148c;
